Full job description
This role will require applicants to be on site 3 days a week and working remotely during after-hours.

Onsite/Remote Desktop Support Technician provides support to customer’s End Users both in person, over the phone, and through Jira ServiceDesk Ticketing system. Technician is responsible for problem determination, problem/incident recording, and problem resolution for clients of GenCon Services, LLC .

Onsite Desktop Support Technicians typically work on-location within a GenCon client’s facilities. The technician will be the direct contact for the initial service ticket request, direct end-user escalations, as well as participate, as instructed, as part of the ServiceDesk call queue and including Systems/Infrastructure team for onsite projects.

The ideal candidate will also have the opportunity to work with our Systems/Infrastructure Engineering team for current and future projects, and will have both exposure and hands-on to VMware, HyperV, Microsoft RDS/VDI, Cyber Security Products, Network Technologies (i.e. Meraki, Unifi, Juniper, Cisco), and other technologies.

This role is a long-term contract position only.

Key Responsibilities

Resolve problems reported to GenCon via phone, jira web tickets or escalations – 50%
Provide Tier 1/2 level support for different clients – Total of 500+ users from different clients
Proactive communications on issue status and resolution to all clients
Maintain ticket updates for all reported incidents.
Review and update Help Desk documentation, and create documentation as needed
Other functions as directed by management (i.e. Infrastructure/Colo projects, VOIP Migrations to MS Teams) – 30% or as pre-determined by client’s needs.
Travel to remote sites with 45 minutes from home office will be required one day a week.
Maintains SLA to all clients and escalate as needed
Works closely with Systems/Infrastructure Engineer with current or future projects
Install and configure/image desktops or laptops
Continuously improve upon soft skill sets required to deliver outstanding customer service
Customer Service Oriented - “Walk-In” activities for any employees that need technical assistance while onsite
